    "rawText": "10-DAY RWANDA DISCOVERY EXPERIENCE \n \nKigali City  - Akagera National Park - Nyungwe Forest - Mountain Gorillas - Community \n \u200b\n \n \nOVERVIEW:  \n \nMurakaza neza! Welcome to Rwanda, a magical landscape of a thousand hills and a million smiling faces. \nWith 26,388Km2 of size, 14 million people of which 70% are below 35 years of age, this small young and yet \nambitious country would give you a shock of life. Etched into global consciousness by the brutality of the \n1994 genocide, the social and economic repair that has occurred since is nothing short of miraculous, the \ncountry is stable, with a track record as the fastest growing in Africa and tourism once again a key contributor \nto the economy. Primate safaris may be the primary drawcard for the country but it\u2019s not all monkey business; \ngo beyond the gorillas, step into an adventure playground waiting to be discovered by the active traveler and \nexperience a country breathtaking in its beauty and graced by a people generous in their welcome. \n \nTRIP HIGHLIGHTS  \n\u25cf Kigali City Tour to learn Rwanda's dark past and journey to present glory  \n\u25cf Wildlife Safari Experience in Akagera National Park \n\u25cf Cultural Experience in Nyanza for pre-colonial history \n\u25cf Chimpanzee Trekking in Nyungwe Forest \n\u25cf Lake Kivu Experience with a blend of relaxation and adventure \n\u25cf Gorilla Trekking Experience in the Volcanoes National Park \n \n \nImportant Arrival notes:  \n\u25cf ALL Visas are obtained upon arrival at Kigali International Airport  \n\u25cf Citizens of the Commonwealth Member Countries DO NOT require a Visa to enter Rwanda and you \nwon\u2019t need ANY vaccines, not the yellow fever or any other vaccine. \n\u25cf Please travel with at least a SIX MONTHS Valid Passport.  \n\u25cf Please refrain from bringing plastic bags to Rwanda. Banned by law since 2008, any plastic bags in your \nluggage would be confiscated at the airport.  \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \nAddress: KN5, Kigali-Rwanda | Tel: +250788615233 | Email:info@luxehorizonsafrica.com | Web: www.luxehorizonsafrica.com \n\n\n \nDAILY PROGRAM\u200b\n\u200b\n\u200b\n\u200b\n\u200b\n\u200b\n\u200b\n\u200b\n                     9 Nights \nDAY 1: ARRIVAL IN RWANDA - AT THE KIGALI INTERNATIONAL AIRPORT \n\u00b7   Arrive in Kigali - Please advise flight details \n\u00b7   Meet & Greet at Airport (Assist with immigration formalities, luggage & escort to the exit) \n\u00b7   Meet your guide & embark on a Private transfer to the Hotel (approx 20min drive) \n\u00b7   Overnight in Kigali - Four to Five star accommodation options \n \n \nDAY 2: KIGALI CITY TOUR - HISTORICAL RWANDA - AKAGERA NATIONAL PARK BOAT CRUISE \n\u00b7   Breakfast & checkout \n\u00b7   Guided Kigali city tour with a visit to the Genocide memorial: A historical component of the trip, \nlearning on Rwanda's dark past, people's resilience and witness the current success stories \n\u00b7   Embark on a scenic drive to Akagera National Park - Home of the Safari Big 5, for approx 3hrs drive \n\u00b7   Sunset Boat ride on the Lake for Crocodiles, Hippos, Birds, visiting Elephants, Giraffes & more \n\u00b7   Overnight within Akagera (Full board) - Four to Five star accommodation options \n \n \nDAY 3: AKAGERA NATIONAL PARK -  FULL DAY SAFARI GAME DRIVE \n\u00b7   Breakfast  \n\u00b7   Full day Safari game drive in search for The Big 5 (Lion, Leopard, Elephant, Buffalo, and Rhino)  \n   and other fascinating species as well, such as giraffes, zebras, antelopes, and a wide variety of birdlife. \n\u00b7   Picnic lunch within the Park and carry on the game drives \n\u00b7   Overnight within Akagera (Full Board) - Four to Five star accommodation options \n \n \nAddress: KN5, Kigali-Rwanda | Tel: +250788615233 | Email:info@luxehorizonsafrica.com | Web: www.luxehorizonsafrica.com \n\n\n \nDAY 4: CULTURAL DRIVE TO NYANZA \n\u00b7   Breakfast  \n\u00b7   Check-out from the hotel \n\u00b7   Drive to Nyanza for approx.4hrs total drive via Kigali \n\u00b7   Cultural community engagement session at the property \n\u00b7   Overnight in Nyanza (Full Board) - Four star accommodation option \n \n \nDAY 5: CAPTIVATING DRIVE TO THE NYUNGWE NATIONAL PARK \n\u00b7  Breakfast  \n\u00b7  Check-out from the hotel \n\u00b7  Visit the King's palace for Rwanda's precolonial history & the long horned \"Inyambo\" Royal cows  \n\u00b7  Embark on a 4hr captivating drive to the majestic Nyungwe National Park \n\u00b7  Evening leisure/relaxation at the property \n\u00b7  Overnight in Nyungwe Forest (Full Board) - Four to Five star accommodation options \n \n \nDAY 6: CHIMPS TREK/CANOPY WALK \n.   Early breakfast \u00b7 5:00AM \n.   Chimpanzee trekking experience \n\u00b7   Lunch at the resort \n\u00b7   Canopy walk ( Suspended bridge walk-way on 70 meters above the forest) \n\u00b7   Optional activities at the lodge (Massage, bird watching, outdoor fire place, etc..)  \n\u00b7   Overnight in Nyungwe Forest (Full Board) - Four to Five star accommodation options \n \nAddress: KN5, Kigali-Rwanda | Tel: +250788615233 | Email:info@luxehorizonsafrica.com | Web: www.luxehorizonsafrica.com \n\n\n \nDAY 7: PANORAMIC DRIVE TO KIBUYE \n\u00b7  Breakfast & Morning Leisure \n\u00b7  Check-out from the hotel \n\u00b7  Embark on a scenic drive to lake Kivu for approx. 4hrs total drive \n\u00b7  Evening Leisure at the beach with the lake views \n\u00b7  Overnight at Lake Kivu (Full Board) - Four to Five star accommodation options \n \n \nDAY 8: KAYAKING ON THE LAKE - PICTURESQUE DRIVE TO THE VOLCANOES \n.  Breakfast  \n\u00b7   Morning Guided Kayaking on Lake Kivu towards historical Kivu Islands \n\u00b7  Embark on a scenic drive to the volcanoes for approx. 5.5hrs via Kigali \n\u00b7  Optional stop-over lunch in Kigali  \n\u00b7  Evening Leisure at the foothills of the volcanoes \n\u00b7  Overnight by the Volcanoes (Full board) - Four to Five star accommodation options \n \n \nDAY 9: MEET THE LEGENDS: GORILLA TREK \n\u00b7  Early Breakfast & head to the park office for briefing and group assigning \n\u00b7  Go Gorilla Trek: The entire experience takes 3 to 7hrs inclusive of 1hr allowed to spend with Gorillas,  \nas they live their life: The Alfa male - Silverback leading the way, the mother looking after the little ones, \nwhile the black-backs (juveniles) are fighting and annoying everybody, just as any other human young \nsiblings! \n\u00b7  Optional afternoon Twin lakes excursions that offers a serene and picturesque experience \n\u00b7  Optional activities at the lodge (Massage, bird watching, outdoor fire place, etc..)  \n\u00b7  Overnight by the Volcanoes (Full board) - Four to Five star accommodation options \nAddress: KN5, Kigali-Rwanda | Tel: +250788615233 | Email:info@luxehorizonsafrica.com | Web: www.luxehorizonsafrica.com \n\n\n \n \n \nDAY 10: KIGALI/ DEPARTURE \n\u00b7  Breakfast & checkout \n\u00b7  Embark on a scenic drive to Kigali for approx 3hrs total drive \n\u00b7  Optional Kigali activities/souvenirs shopping  \n\u00b7  Airport transfer & Depart Rwanda - TBA \n \nEND OF TOUR \n \n \n \nAddress: KN5, Kigali-Rwanda | Tel: +250788615233 | Email:info@luxehorizonsafrica.com | Web: www.luxehorizonsafrica.com"
